Host-side gtest unit tests for crosspoint-reader.

Build and run:

  cmake -S test -B build/test
  cmake --build build/test
  ctest --test-dir build/test --output-on-failure -j

Run a single suite directly:

  cmake --build build/test --target StreamingJsonParserTest
  build/test/streaming_json_parser/StreamingJsonParserTest --gtest_filter='*'

Google Test is fetched via CMake FetchContent on first configure; the pinned
version lives in test/CMakeLists.txt.

Shared pieces:

  cmake/HostThemeStack.cmake  crosspoint_add_theme_stack(target repo_root) links
                              the REAL UITheme + BaseTheme/Lyra/Lyra3Covers/
                              LyraSix chain host-side. Needed by any suite whose
                              code reads GUI — which includes activity onEnter/
                              loop paths, not just render().
  host_stubs/                 The headers that chain needs and only that:
                              HalClock.h, HalPowerManager.h (their real versions
                              reach ESP-IDF) and WString.h (FsHelpers.h wants
                              Arduino's String). Suite-specific seams — HalGPIO,
                              HalStorage — stay in each suite's own stubs/.

test/activity_input additionally needs ArduinoJson, which comes from PlatformIO's
lib_deps rather than the repo, so run any `pio run` once before configuring.
